So you assigned the species tags as, for example, "Species|Spotted_deer", not "Spotted_deer"?

In other words, in your digiKam tag tree, does it look something like in the example in the vignette (the image here <https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/camtrapR/vignettes/SpeciesIndividualIdentification.html#metadata-tag-structure>)? Or would the tags in the example read "Species|Leopard Cat", "Species|Spotted_deer" etc? If that was the case, you'd need to remove the "Species|" part in the tag manager and refresh the image metadata (using the "Write metadata to Images" button).
Also, when you use metadata tags, you can safely use spaces (Spotted deer instead of Spotted_deer).

But before you do anything, would you mind sharing a screenshot of your digiKam metadata tag tree please? Just to be sure I'm giving you the right advise. Or share a tagged sample image, then I can check the metadata.

Jürgen

